  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Electric Boat obligated $11.6B in FY2026 to date. Electric Boat received 333 awards during the period, with an average award size of $34.8M. Electric Boat obligations are down 45.8% year over year. Electric Boat obligations peaked at $21.4B in FY25 and rose from $8.7B in FY21 to $10.8B in FY23 before the FY25 jump and the current-year decline. Electric Boat activity is concentrated in a few industries: Engineering Services received $7B and Ship Building and Repairing received $4.6B in FY2026 to date, followed by smaller amounts in specialized manufacturing and research categories. Electric Boat figures shown are contract obligations except where award values are identified as total contract values in the underlying tables, and current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date).",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How do FY2026 obligations compare with recent years?",
        "body": "Electric Boat obligated $11.6B in FY26 to date, down 45.8% year over year. Electric Boat obligations varied by fiscal year: FY21 $8.7B, FY22 $9.4B, FY23 $10.8B, FY24 $8.6B, and FY25 $21.4B. Electric Boat FY25 totals are the largest on record in the provided series, and FY26 totals are partial (fiscal year to date)."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which markets drive Electric Boat revenue in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "Engineering Services is the largest market for Electric Boat with $7B in obligations in FY2026 to date. Ship Building and Repairing follows with $4.6B. Electric Boat also has obligations in Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) at $3.4M and several manufacturing niches ranging from $2.4M down to $464K."
      }
    ]
  },
